WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
<b>Calpis theater</b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Subs: English

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
S

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
<b><i>SILVER ZERO
 SUBS</i></b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
http://silverzerosubs.blogspot.com/

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
Original story by Johanna Spyri

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
<b>Alps no Shoujo Heidi</b>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
<u>Why do I hear</u>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
Kuchibue ha naze

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
<u>the whistling from far away?</u>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
<u>Why is that cloud</u>

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
Ano kumo ha naze

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
<u>waiting for me?</u>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
Watashi wo matteru no

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
<u>Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm.</u>

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.580
Whistle Louder

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:40.160
Hey, Peter, you never come
to play with us anymore.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.360
Peter prefers to play with the weird
granddaughter of Alm-Uncle.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.580
Oh, you're talking about Heidi.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.180
Yes, isn't that right?

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.270
She's not weird.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:54.880
Yes, she is. Or else she wouldn't
live up there with Alm-Uncle.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.250
That's not true!

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.850
Yes, it is.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:01.290
And she has a beard like Alm-Uncle.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.780
She has not.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:07.780
If you don't stop playing with her,
you will also have a beard.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.600
You're really an idiot.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.080
What?

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.200
Peter has a beard!

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.140
Good morning, Peter.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.670
I'll leave my goat in your care.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:30.490
Yes.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:33.300
What about that girl?
How is Heidi?

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.520
She says she wants to be a goatherd.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.160
A goatherd?

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.020
Let's go!

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.940
That boy must be having a hard time.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:58.160
I'm sure Alm-Uncle makes
him look after the girl.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.930
Good morning, Pichi.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.690
Good morning.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.540
Pichi, don't go far away.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.250
Little Swan, Little Bear,
good morning.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.310
You're already awake?

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.330
Let me do that, Grandfather.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:14.070
I decided that I want to be a
goatherd as good as Peter.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.810
But can you milk a goat?

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.150
I can. I really can.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:20.420
I wonder.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.450
I can do it.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:32.880
Well, here I go.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.010
Nothing comes out.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.330
Maybe like this?

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.540
Very well. This time I will do it.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:58.660
Looks like you'll need a bigger bucket.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.550
It's because Little Swan doesn't stand still.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.870
It may look like it's easy,
but it's surprisingly difficult.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:09.080
Don't worry. This time I'll do it.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.800
Little Swan, don't move so much.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.760
This time...

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:22.790
I did it!

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:26.360
Little Swan!

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.250
Little Bear!

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.710
Stop doing that!

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.930
Stop. Stop that.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:37.870
W-w-what's wrong?

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:40.670
What is it?

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.240
What's wrong?

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.230
Little Bear is jealous.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.920
Jealous?

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.130
Yes, she too wants to be milked by you.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:57.420
Little Swan, what do you want?

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.370
What is it, Little Bear?

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:03.240
Grandfather, help me!

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.090
You two.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:08.780
Go, go.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:16.620
Like I thought, I should do it.
Come, Little Bear.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:27.500
I just needed a little more time.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.530
Peter, good morning!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.100
Good morning!

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.800
Snowflake, don't stay behind.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:08.520
Did you listen? You did, right?
I whistled, didn't I?

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.330
You still need to practice more.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.110
I don't.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.610
Nothing's coming out.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.080
I'm going first.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:32.560
Wait!

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:42.000
<i>At the same time, the old man
prepares for a trip down the mountain.</i>

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:43.910
<i>It's been a while since the last time.</i>

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:46.720
<i>Grandfather is bringing bowls and spoons</i>

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:51.030
<i>that he as carved out of the
hardwood that grows in high places.</i>

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:55.800
<i>He's also bringing cheese that he has made</i>

00:08:55.980 --> 00:09:00.000
<i>to exchange for bread and other foods.</i>

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.730
Well, then...

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.110
Well, I'm going.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.690
All right, Joseph?

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.890
Shall we eat now?

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:36.930
Is it time already?

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.870
Look, the sun is above us.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:44.450
Pichi, let's eat!

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:50.610
You understood that, Pichi?

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.670
Wait. Wait!

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.820
Let me call them.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:06.450
Wait a little.

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:08.170
I'll call them.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.370
Come on, everyone!

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:17.080
Follow me!

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.720
Everyone, come here!

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:29.180
Come on, let's go.

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:43.490
You can't do it that way!
You're just gonna scare them.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:46.470
I know!

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:51.280
You need to count them first
to take them home, don't you?

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:53.400
Yes, can you do it?

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:54.850
Yes, I can.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:21.280
Oh? Too many?

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:27.230
That's right, I counted Greenfinch before.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:29.610
I'm going to count them again!

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:32.020
You don't need to!
I already counted them!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:33.840
How did you do it?

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:37.420
You don't need to go to them!
You can count them better if you are far away!

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:39.900
I see.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.230
Little Swan!

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.160
Let me do it.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:46.120
All right?

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:48.490
No. No.
You can't do it.

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:52.120
I can. All right?
Let me milk my goat.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:55.670
But you told me you couldn't do it this morning.

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.800
That's because she wouldn't stand still.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:03.050
Do what you want.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:07.330
But I don't think you'll be able to do it,
just like you still don't know how to whistle.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.660
Then teach me.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.680
Teach me how to do it.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:14.170
Impossible.

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:19.610
Very well.

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:22.480
Today I won't give you my bread and cheese.

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:24.290
Eh? Oh, no...

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:27.630
All right, I'll teach you how to do it.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.140
That's great!

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:40.840
It's been a while.

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:45.050
You were a friend of his son, weren't you?
Why don't you say something to him?

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:50.000
No. I wouldn't want to get him in a bad mood.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.200
Well, that's true.

00:12:57.300 --> 00:13:01.610
Look. It's Alm-Uncle.
He came down the mountain.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:04.040
Does he bring the girl with him?

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:05.300
No, he doesn't.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:09.650
Could he have left her alone up there?

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:17.200
It's Alm-Uncle.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:19.390
It really is!

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:28.830
Hello, Neighbor. You look good as always.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:30.880
You seem well, too.

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:34.920
Why don't you come to the church sometime?

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:36.720
Sorry, I'm busy.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.520
What's wrong with him?
That old fool.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:44.270
Poor child.
He left Heidi alone up there.

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.180
That's why I tried to warn Dete.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:50.410
She was wrong to trust her
niece to that horrible Alm-Uncle.

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:03.610
Welcome.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.120
It's been a while.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.600
The same bread as usual?

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:13.900
That's right.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:17.440
The same as usual.
How are things up there?

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.310
Here you go.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:23.820
It's not right.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:26.610
The amount of bread is not right.

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:29.080
No, this is what you get for the cheese.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:33.730
What? I may live in the mountains
but I know how to count.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:37.360
No. That's the right amount.
Isn't that right, dear?

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:42.270
Oh, I remember now! The price of bread rose
since the last time he came here.

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:43.790
That's true!

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:46.790
You come here so infrequently.

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:50.790
I see. You think I'm crazy
because I come here so rarely?

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.060
No, we don't!

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:55.010
You are trying to fool me!

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:57.980
Trying to fool you?
How dare you say such things?

00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:01.140
Everyone around here knows
that we are very honest people.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.130
We won't sell you any more
bread if you continue.

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:06.480
All right. Very well.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:11.900
Enough. I'll buy my bread in Mayenfeld.
We won't do business anymore.

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:20.570
What a terrible old man.

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:23.420
I never thought he was that crazy.
My goodness.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:47.850
<i>After his argument
with the baker at Dorfli,</i>

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:52.550
<i>Grandfather goes to Mayenfeld to buy bread.</i>

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:54.530
<i>Unlike the small village,</i>

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:58.800
<i>here there are many shops
where he can buy various things.</i>

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:13.740
It hurts.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.530
Peter, are you all right?

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.350
Aren't you feeling well?

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:20.940
My belly hurts a lot.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:22.490
What should I do?

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:25.310
That's because you ate too much cheese.

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:28.160
Ow-ow-ow!

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:31.920
I don't have a choice.
I have to gather the herd.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.460
How do I do it?

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.720
Little Swan, Little Bear,
Don't do that!

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:55.650
Peter, Little Swan and
Little Bear are going to fall!

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.400
Then call them!

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:01.220
Call them fast!

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:04.750
What's wrong?
Where are you going?

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:07.700
Don't ask me that.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.850
Stop that! Stop fighting!

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:23.810
Stop at once.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.660
Stop that, Little Swan!
Little Swan!

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:34.170
Stop that!

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:42.800
Little Bear!
Little Bear!

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:16.730
Idiots.
Idiots.

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:19.480
Little Swan and Little Bear, you idiots!
Idiots, idiots!

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:25.130
I shouldn't have eaten so much.

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:29.570
You managed to call them.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:36.950
No, I'm still not a good goatherd.

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:42.280
I don't even know... how to whistle.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:48.910
I did it! I whistled!

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.240
Good, good!

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:56.080
I can whistle!
I know how to whistle!

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:26.470
Peter, look.
The goats are coming to me.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:27.900
You did it.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:29.090
Snowflake.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:30.600
Pichi.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:35.050
Now I can be a goatherd!
Now everyone can hear me whistle!

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:02.370
Joseph!

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.650
I'm back!
Grandfather, I'm back!

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.300
Grandfather!

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.890
He's not home.

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:21.890
He must be in the village.

00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:23.160
In the village?

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:26.810
Be quiet.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:30.110
To do what?

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.610
To trade his cheese for bread.

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:35.280
I see, to get bread.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.410
Oh, Goat General.

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.340
I was right, he was in the village.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:54.440
Is Heidi at home?

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:56.600
She just arrived.

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:57.600
I see...

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:10.340
Stand still, all right?

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:14.140
I'm going to milk you to surprise Grandfather.

00:21:26.980 --> 00:21:27.960
Grandfather.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:29.400
Welcome back.

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:32.590
I can milk.
I know how to milk.

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:35.320
Peter taught me how to do it on the mountain.

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.440
Look how much I milked.

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:43.930
Look at me doing it.

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:52.350
See.
I do it very well, don't I?

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:54.520
You do.
You do it really well.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:59.470
I also learned one more thing.
Now I know how to whistle.

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:06.000
Grandfather, can you do it?

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:09.480
Yes, I also know to whistle.

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:10.830
Then show me.

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:12.640
All right.

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:19.940
You do it so well.
Do it again.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.400
I'm going to join you.

00:22:31.400 --> 00:22:32.400
All right.

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:40.690
Lovely, lovely.
It was really loud.

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:44.440
All right, I will prepare dinner.

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:48.480
I bought delicious bread
and a good piece of meat.

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:49.480
Really?

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:51.360
And also...

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:53.600
Here, I brought you this.

00:22:56.200 --> 00:22:58.040
Thank you, Grandfather.

00:22:59.800 --> 00:23:02.470
It looks delicious.
Can I taste a little?

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:04.730
Of course.

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:10.370
It's so sweet!
It seems to melt on the tongue!

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:15.300
Well, dinner will be ready soon.
Go wash your hands.

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:16.540
Yes.

00:23:24.550 --> 00:23:28.650
<i>Heidi is now truly a child of the mountain.</i>

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:30.940
<i>And the old man</i>

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:35.880
<i>can no longer imagine a life
on the mountain without Heidi.</i>

00:23:54.970 --> 00:23:58.920
<i>On the Alm Mountain,
the days continue to be windy.</i>

00:23:59.110 --> 00:24:02.630
<i>That's because fall is just around the corner.</i>

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:05.580
<i>Heidi isn't allowed to go up the mountain,</i>

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:09.060
<i>so she helps her grandfather to make cheese.</i>

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:13.390
<i>Heidi completely forgets the mountain.</i>

00:24:13.940 --> 00:24:18.510
<i>However, one day Snowflake comes
back from the mountain alone.</i>

00:24:18.510 --> 00:24:21.940
<i>When Heidi tries to bring Snowflake
back up the mountain,</i>

00:24:21.950 --> 00:24:25.700
<i>the wind is blowing and she
hears the sound of the fir trees.</i>

00:24:25.860 --> 00:24:28.550
<i>Next episode:
The Sound of the Fir Trees</i>

00:24:28.550 --> 00:24:30.150
<i>Please look forward to it!</i>

